          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "For drafting estate planning documents in **Logan** and the **Western Corridor (Ipswich, Greater Springfield, and Western Brisbane)**, it is essential to work with a practitioner experienced in Queensland succession law—particularly for **Testamentary Discretionary Trusts (TDTs)** and **Enduring Powers of Attorney (EPOAs)** under the *Powers of Attorney Act 1998 (QLD)*.\n\nThe top-rated and most established firms and lawyers in these regions are outlined below by territory:\n\n---\n\n### **1. Western Corridor (Ipswich, Greater Springfield & Brookwater)**\n\n* **Fallu McMillan Lawyers (Ipswich)**  \n  * **Profile:** One of Ipswich’s longest-established and most respected law firms.  \n  * **Strengths:** Dedicated wills and estates practice handling everything from standard wills to complex testamentary trusts and succession planning. They are experienced in asset protection, blended family planning, and tailored EPOAs.\n* **McNamara Law (Ipswich & Springfield Central)**  \n  * **Profile:** A major regional firm with substantial resources and multiple offices along the western corridor.  \n  * **Strengths:** Excellent for clients with broader commercial assets, business succession considerations, or property portfolios tied into their estate plan. They offer structured estate planning, including testamentary trusts and health/financial attorney appointments.\n* **Brookwater Legal / Keane Legal (Brookwater & Greater Springfield)**  \n  * **Profile:** Conveniently located in the Springfield/Brookwater corridor, targeting growing families, professionals, and retirees in the western master-planned communities.  \n  * **Strengths:** Strong focus on modern estate planning. They frequently draft testamentary trusts designed for tax efficiency (allowing income splitting for minor children) and bankruptcy/divorce protection.\n* **Jacaranda Law (Ipswich)**  \n  * **Profile:** A boutique practice that focuses exclusively on wills, trusts, and estate administration.  \n  * **Strengths:** Because their core practice is succession law, they specialize heavily in testamentary trust wills, clear plain-English drafting, and structured EPOAs, often on a transparent, fixed-fee basis.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Logan Region (Springwood, Beenleigh & Loganholme)**\n\n* **Turner Freeman Lawyers (Logan / Springwood Office)**  \n  * **Profile:** A national firm with a strong local presence in Springwood and Ipswich, consistently recognized by *Doyle’s Guide* for estate matters.  \n  * **Strengths:** They have access to accredited specialists and senior estate practitioners who handle both contentious and non-contentious succession law. Highly recommended if you anticipate potential challenges to your will or need advanced estate protection.\n* **Ryder Lawyers (Beenleigh & Logan)**  \n  * **Profile:** A boutique firm with a strong focus on family law, elder law, and succession planning across Logan and northern Gold Coast corridors.  \n  * **Strengths:** Significant experience with testamentary trusts, complex family arrangements, granny flat agreements, and ensuring EPOAs prevent elder financial abuse.\n* **McLaughlin & Associates Lawyers (Springwood)**  \n  * **Profile:** A long-standing Logan practice with decades of experience handling property, trusts, and commercial law alongside private client estates.  \n  * **Strengths:** Ideal for business owners and family trust controllers in Logan who need their personal wills and testamentary trusts aligned with corporate entities and family trust deeds.\n* **SKC Lawyers (Logan City)**  \n  * **Profile:** A local firm providing clear, accessible estate planning and estate administration services across the Logan region.  \n  * **Strengths:** Focused on practical asset protection, drafting testamentary trusts, Advance Health Directives (AHDs), and EPOAs.\n\n---\n\n### **Key Considerations Before Booking a Consultation**\n\nWhen setting up testamentary trusts and enduring powers of attorney, make sure to ask prospective solicitors the following:\n\n1. **Fixed Fees vs. Hourly Rates:** Most firms offer fixed-fee packages for a *comprehensive estate planning pack* (Will with Testamentary Trust + EPOA + Advance Health Directive). Get an upfront quote for both single and mirror/spousal wills.\n2. **Accreditation and Professional Memberships:** Ask if the supervising lawyer is a **Queensland Law Society (QLS) Accredited Specialist in Succession Law** or a member of **STEP** (Society of Trust and Estate Practitioners). This is particularly critical for high-net-worth estates, self-managed super funds (SMSFs), or family businesses.\n3. **Superannuation & Non-Estate Assets:** Ensure the lawyer assesses assets that **do not automatically form part of your will**, such as superannuation death benefit nominations (BDBNs) and assets held in family discretionary trusts or company names.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
